/* data/detail-c/mth-12-09.js - GENERATED by tools/build.py from data/detail/mth-12-09.json (our own words). Do not edit. */
(window.DETAIL_C = window.DETAIL_C || {})["mth-12-09"] = {"mth-12-09-m01":{"idea":"The derivative is a rate of change.","steps":["dy/dx measures how fast y changes when x changes by a small amount.","If x is time, it is the speed at which y changes.","So it is the rate of change of y with respect to x."],"others":"The area under a curve needs an integral. The value of x where y is zero is a root. The total change over an interval is Δy, not a rate.","trap":"Derivative is rate, integral is accumulation.","answer":"the rate of change of y with respect to x"},"mth-12-09-m02":{"idea":"Write the area in terms of r, then use the chain rule with time.","steps":["A = πr².","Differentiate with respect to t: dA/dt = 2πr × dr/dt.","At a bigger radius the same dr/dt adds more area."],"others":"πr² dr/dt does not lower the power. 2π dr/dt drops the factor r. π dr/dt has neither factor.","trap":"Differentiate r² to 2r, then times dr/dt.","answer":"dA/dt = 2πr (dr/dt)"},"mth-12-09-m03":{"idea":"Write the volume as a power of the side.","steps":["The volume of a cube is V = s³.","Differentiate with time: dV/dt = 3s² × ds/dt.","The power drops by one and the old power comes in front."],"others":"6s dr is not from V = s³. 3s ds/dt lowers the power too far. s³ ds/dt does not differentiate at all. The surface area 6s² would give 12s ds/dt.","trap":"Do not mix volume and surface area.","answer":"dV/dt = 3s² (ds/dt)"},"mth-12-09-m04":{"idea":"Increasing means the graph rises, so the slope is positive.","steps":["The slope of the graph is f'(x).","If f'(x) > 0 on an interval, the graph rises as x increases.","A negative f'(x) means the function is decreasing."],"others":"Negative f' means decreasing. Positive f'' tells about bending, not rising. A positive value of f(x) only says the graph is above the axis.","trap":"First derivative decides rise and fall.","answer":"f'(x) is positive"},"mth-12-09-m05":{"idea":"Find the sign of f' on each side of the turning point.","steps":["f'(x) = 2x − 4 = 2(x − 2).","For x below 2 this is negative, so f decreases.","For x above 2 it is positive, so f increases. The minimum is at x = 2."],"others":"A parabola that opens up cannot decrease everywhere or increase everywhere. The last option reverses the true pattern.","trap":"The sign of the slope flips at the vertex.","answer":"decreasing for x less than 2, and increasing for x greater than 2"},"mth-12-09-m06":{"idea":"Critical points are the candidates for local extremes.","steps":["Set f'(x) = 0, or look for points where f' does not exist.","Those are the critical points.","They need not be maxima or minima, as x³ at 0 shows."],"others":"f(x) = 0 is a root. f'' = 0 alone is for inflection candidates. The largest value in the domain is the absolute maximum.","trap":"Critical does not always mean extreme.","answer":"f'(x) = 0 or f'(x) does not exist"},"mth-12-09-m07":{"idea":"A peak means the function goes up, then down.","steps":["Before c, the function rises, so f' is positive.","After c, the function falls, so f' is negative.","A sign change from positive to negative gives a local maximum."],"others":"Negative to negative and positive to positive mean no change, so neither a maximum nor a minimum. Negative to positive gives a local minimum.","trap":"Plus to minus is a peak.","answer":"from positive to negative as x passes through c"},"mth-12-09-m08":{"idea":"A negative second derivative means the curve bends downward.","steps":["Suppose f′ at c = 0.","If f″ at c < 0 the curve is concave down, like a cap, so c is a local maximum.","If f″ at c > 0 it is a minimum. If f″ at c = 0 the test fails."],"others":"The third derivative does not decide this. f'' equal to 0 gives no answer. A positive f'' gives a minimum.","trap":"Cap is maximum, cup is minimum.","answer":"f''(c) is negative"},"mth-12-09-m09":{"idea":"This is the extreme value theorem.","steps":["A continuous function on a closed interval cannot escape to infinity.","So it reaches a largest and a smallest value.","Compare the values at the critical points and at the two end points."],"others":"Saying it need not have extremes is false for closed intervals. The maximum may also be inside. Having a maximum but not a minimum is not possible here.","trap":"Closed and continuous gives both.","answer":"has both an absolute maximum and an absolute minimum on the interval"},"mth-12-09-m10":{"idea":"A horizontal tangent has zero slope.","steps":["The slope of the tangent is f'(x).","A line parallel to the x-axis has slope 0.","So f'(x) = 0 at that point."],"others":"If f' does not exist, the tangent may be vertical. f' = 1 gives a 45° line. f(x) = 0 means the curve touches the axis, not that the tangent is flat.","trap":"Horizontal means slope zero.","answer":"f'(x) = 0"},"mth-12-09-m11":{"idea":"Near a point, the tangent line is a good copy of the curve.","steps":["The slope of the tangent is f'(x).","A small step Δx changes the tangent's height by f'(x) Δx.","So Δy ≈ f'(x) Δx, which is called dy."],"others":"Dividing by the slope inverts the relation. f'' is used for second order corrections. The product f(x) Δx has no meaning as a change.","trap":"Slope times step.","answer":"f'(x) Δx, which is the differential dy"},"mth-12-09-m12":{"idea":"Use the tangent at a nearby easy point.","steps":["Take f(x) = √x at x = 25, with Δx = 0.2.","f'(25) = 1/(2√25) = 0.1.","√25.2 ≈ 5 + 0.1 × 0.2 = 5.02."],"others":"5.002 puts the decimal one place too far. 5.04 doubles the correction. 5.2 adds the whole 0.2 as if the slope were 1.","trap":"The slope of √x at 25 is 0.1, not 1.","answer":"5.02"},"mth-12-09-m13":{"idea":"Same height at both ends means a flat tangent somewhere in between.","steps":["The graph starts and ends at the same height.","So it has a peak or a valley between the ends.","At that point the tangent is horizontal: f′ at c = 0 for some c in the interval."],"others":"The theorem does not say f' is zero everywhere. It does not say f is constant. It does not promise a root of f.","trap":"At least one point, not all points.","answer":"there is a point c in (a, b) with f'(c) = 0"},"mth-12-09-m14":{"idea":"Somewhere the instantaneous rate equals the average rate.","steps":["The average rate over the interval is (f at b − f at a)/(b − a).","The theorem says some point c in between has this slope.","Geometrically, a tangent is parallel to the chord joining the end points."],"others":"f′ at c = 0 is Rolle's special case. An average of the end values is not a slope. The plain difference f at b − f at a forgets to divide by the length.","trap":"Divide the change by b − a.","answer":"f'(c) = (f(b) − f(a))/(b − a)"},"mth-12-09-m15":{"idea":"Inflection means the bending switches direction.","steps":["Concave up means bending like a cup, concave down like a cap.","At an inflection point the curve changes from one to the other.","So f'' changes sign there, as x³ does at 0."],"others":"A local maximum or minimum is about slope, not bending. A horizontal tangent at all points belongs to a constant function.","trap":"Inflection is a change of concavity.","answer":"the concavity of the curve changes"},"mth-12-09-m16":{"idea":"Fix the perimeter, write the area with one variable, and maximise.","steps":["Let the perimeter be 2p and one side x. The other side is p − x.","Area = x(p − x), a parabola that opens downward.","Its maximum is at x = p/2, so both sides are equal, which is a square."],"others":"A largest rectangle does exist. A length twice the width gives a smaller area. A long thin one has a small area.","trap":"For a fixed perimeter, the square wins.","answer":"the square"},"mth-12-09-m17":{"idea":"A zero slope is only a candidate for an extreme.","steps":["f'(x) = 3x² is zero at x = 0.","It is positive on both sides, so the sign does not change.","So there is no maximum or minimum, only a flat spot, a point of inflection."],"others":"A zero slope alone does not make a minimum or maximum. The function is increasing everywhere, so it has no absolute minimum.","trap":"Check the sign change.","answer":"neither a maximum nor a minimum, but a point of inflection"},"mth-12-09-m18":{"idea":"Velocity is the rate of change of position, and acceleration of velocity.","steps":["v = ds/dt.","a = dv/dt = d²s/dt².","The particle is at rest for an instant when v = 0."],"others":"The square of ds/dt is not the acceleration. Swapping the two gives the wrong names. s/t is only an average speed.","trap":"Each step is one more derivative.","answer":"ds/dt and d²s/dt²"},"mth-12-09-m19":{"idea":"Factor the derivative and check its sign.","steps":["f'(x) = 6x² − 18x + 12 = 6(x − 1)(x − 2).","It is positive when x < 1 or x > 2.","It is negative between 1 and 2, so the function is increasing only outside that interval."],"others":"Increasing for x below 0 only is not the full answer. It is not increasing everywhere, as f' is negative between 1 and 2. Between 1 and 2 the function decreases.","trap":"Two roots make three intervals.","answer":"x less than 1, and x greater than 2"},"mth-12-09-m20":{"idea":"Differentiate the volume of a sphere.","steps":["V = (4/3)πr³.","dV/dt = (4/3)π × 3r² × dr/dt = 4πr² dr/dt.","That is the surface area times the rate of growth of the radius."],"others":"4πr dr/dt lowers the power too far. (4/3)πr² dr/dt forgets the 3. (4/3)πr³ dr/dt does not differentiate.","trap":"The 3 cancels the 1/3.","answer":"4πr² (dr/dt)"},"mth-12-09-m21":{"idea":"Local means only near the point.","steps":["A local maximum beats the points close to it.","It need not beat points far away.","A function can have several local maxima of different heights."],"others":"A value of zero has nothing to do with it. An end point is not required. The largest value in the whole domain is the absolute maximum.","trap":"Local is not the same as absolute.","answer":"the largest value near the point, but not necessarily the largest overall"},"mth-12-09-m22":{"idea":"Write the volume in terms of the cut size x.","steps":["Cut squares of side x from each corner of a sheet of side a.","The base is a square of side a − 2x and the height is x.","So V = x(a − 2x)². Setting V' = 0 gives x = a/6."],"others":"(a − 2x)² forgets the height. x(a − x)² uses the wrong base side. x²(a − 2x) mixes the sides.","trap":"Two cuts per side: a − 2x.","answer":"V(x) = x(a − 2x)², where x is the side of the squares cut off"},"mth-12-09-m23":{"idea":"Marginal cost is the rate of change of cost.","steps":["C(x) is the cost for x items.","dC/dx tells how the cost changes as one more item is made, approximately.","That is the marginal cost."],"others":"The sum of two successive costs is meaningless here. x dC/dx is not a standard quantity. C/x is the average cost.","trap":"Marginal is a derivative, average is a ratio.","answer":"dC/dx, the rate of change of cost with the number of items"},"mth-12-09-m24":{"idea":"Use the second derivative test.","steps":["f′ at a = 0 means a stationary point.","f″ at a > 0 means the curve bends upward, like a cup.","So the point is a local minimum."],"others":"An end point is not given by this test. An inflection needs f'' to change sign. A local maximum needs f'' negative.","trap":"Positive second derivative gives a minimum.","answer":"a local minimum"},"mth-12-09-n01":{"idea":"Differentiate the area with time.","steps":["A = πr², so dA/dt = 2πr dr/dt.","Put r = 5 and dr/dt = 2: 2π × 5 × 2 = 20π.","20π = 62.83 cm²/s."],"trap":"Use the rate 2, not the radius twice.","answer":"62.83"},"mth-12-09-n02":{"idea":"Differentiate the volume with time.","steps":["V = s³, so dV/dt = 3s² ds/dt.","Put s = 4 and ds/dt = 0.5: 3 × 16 × 0.5.","The result is 24 cm³/s."],"trap":"Square the side first.","answer":"24"},"mth-12-09-n03":{"idea":"Find where the slope is zero, then check the sign of f''.","steps":["f'(x) = −2x + 4 = 0 gives x = 2.","f''(x) = −2 is negative, so it is a maximum.","f(2) = −4 + 8 + 5 = 9."],"trap":"Put x back in f, not f'.","answer":"9"},"mth-12-09-n04":{"idea":"Set the derivative to zero and check the sign of f''.","steps":["f'(x) = 2x − 6 = 0 gives x = 3.","f'' = 2 is positive, so it is a minimum.","f(3) = 9 − 18 + 10 = 1."],"trap":"A parabola that opens up has a minimum.","answer":"1"},"mth-12-09-n05":{"idea":"Use dy = f'(x) dx at x = 25.","steps":["f(x) = √x, so f'(x) = 1/(2√x), and at 25 it is 0.1.","dy = 0.1 × 0.2 = 0.02.","√25.2 ≈ 5 + 0.02 = 5.02."],"trap":"Add the small change to the known root.","answer":"5.02"},"mth-12-09-n06":{"idea":"Find the critical points, then test the sign of f''.","steps":["f'(x) = 3x² − 12 = 0 gives x = 2 or x = −2.","f''(x) = 6x is positive at x = 2, so it is a local minimum there.","f(2) = 8 − 24 = −16."],"trap":"At x = −2 there is a local maximum, not the minimum.","answer":"-16"},"mth-12-09-n07":{"idea":"Write the area with one variable.","steps":["Perimeter 40 means the sum of two adjacent sides is 20.","With sides x and 20 − x the area is x(20 − x), which is largest at x = 10.","The largest area is 10 × 10 = 100 cm²."],"trap":"Half the perimeter, not the whole.","answer":"100"},"mth-12-09-n08":{"idea":"Write the volume in terms of x and find its maximum.","steps":["V = x(12 − 2x)².","V' = (12 − 2x)(12 − 6x) = 0 gives x = 6 or x = 2. At x = 6 the volume is zero.","V(2) = 2 × 8² = 128 cm³."],"trap":"Reject the root that gives zero volume.","answer":"128"},"mth-12-09-n09":{"idea":"Set f′ at c equal to the average slope.","steps":["Average slope = (f(3) − f(1))/(3 − 1) = (9 − 1)/2 = 4.","f′ at c = 2c, so 2c = 4.","c = 2, which lies in the interval (1, 3)."],"trap":"Check c lies inside the interval.","answer":"2"},"mth-12-09-n10":{"idea":"Velocity is the derivative of position.","steps":["v = ds/dt = 3t² − 12t + 9.","At t = 2: v = 12 − 24 + 9.","v = −3 m/s, so the particle moves backwards."],"trap":"A negative velocity means moving backwards.","answer":"-3"}};
